# Memory synthesis

Classify evidence into `profile`, `preferences`, `entities`, `events`, `identity`,
`soul`, `cases`, `trajectories`, `experiences`, `tools`, or `skills`. Preserve the
OpenViking YAML field shapes exposed by the bank schema.

1. Recall relevant existing memories before writing.
2. Copy the exact batch ID, complete evidence IDs, and lease owner from the
   current job into every mutation and completion call. Never reuse a lease
   from an earlier job.
3. Use the complete `evidence_ids` set as the server-validated citation for
   every mutation. Mention a source checksum only when explaining a provenance
   conflict; mutation tools do not accept a separate checksum field.
4. Upsert stable facts, use supersede for replaced facts, and use forget only
   when the cited batch proves an existing memory should be removed.
5. Keep Wiki pages, Skills, and Tools canonical in their owning Tilde domain;
   memory stores derived facts and learned usage, not copied control-plane state.
6. Keep user, team, project/task, and agent-learning subjects distinct.
